    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0749" n="1583" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/932</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 18, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 1.24 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4704. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 2122. Embassy’s 4331 of December 5, our 2001;<anchor n="1" xml:id="d625-f1"/>
                    Embassy’s 4423 of December 9, our 2024;<anchor n="1" xml:id="d625-f2"/> and
                    Embassy’s 4648 of December 16, our 2104.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d625-f3"/> N.O.T.
                    agreement has just been signed by representatives of British, French and Italian
                    Governments and N.O.T., although all parties greatly regretted that no answer
                    from War Trade Board has been received to our 2001 which was sent from here 13
                    days ago, yet as Valstar must leave for Holland this morning and as British
                    representatives are to leave for Paris tomorrow negotiations could not be
                    further prolonged here and for the reasons indicated in our above tables it was
                    considered undesirable to leave negotiations in an uncompleted state with
                    probable result that they would be entirely reopened by Dutch Government or
                    N.O.T. at The Hague. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
